<zk xmlns:n="native">
	<zscript><![CDATA[
		java.util.Calendar c = java.util.Calendar.getInstance();
		java.util.Date defaultBegin = c.getTime();
		c.add(java.util.Calendar.DAY_OF_MONTH, 7);
		java.util.Date defaultEnd = c.getTime();
	]]></zscript>
	<n:p>
	Daterangebox (ZK EE, since 11.0.0) lets the user pick a single contiguous
	date range in one component: a begin input on the left, an end input on the
	right, and a calendar popup whose month panels paint the whole selected span.
	It addresses the common "date range picker" need - between two dates, before
	a date, or after a date.
	</n:p>

	<n:h1>Basic</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	two inputs with a calendar popup; by default the popup shows two month panels
	side by side
	</n:p>
	<daterangebox/>

	<n:h1>Separator and placeholders</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	separator is rendered between the two inputs; beginPlaceholder/endPlaceholder
	hint each field
	</n:p>
	<daterangebox separator=" &#8594; "
				  beginPlaceholder="Check-in" endPlaceholder="Check-out"/>

	<n:h1>With time</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	showTime adds a time-picker row per endpoint and appends HH:mm to the inputs
	</n:p>
	<daterangebox showTime="true"/>

	<n:h1>Number of month panels</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	numberOfMonths controls how many calendars the popup shows side by side (1-12)
	</n:p>
	<daterangebox numberOfMonths="1"/>
	<daterangebox numberOfMonths="3"/>

	<n:h1>Range length: minNights / maxNights</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	bound the selectable span in calendar days; a violation raises a
	WrongValueException error box
	</n:p>
	<daterangebox minNights="2" maxNights="14"/>

	<n:h1>Constraint</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	reuses the Datebox constraint syntax, applied to both endpoints
	</n:p>
	<daterangebox constraint="no past"/>
	<daterangebox constraint="after 20260101, before 20261231"/>

	<n:h1>allowEmpty</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	which endpoints may be left empty: none / begin / end / both (default both)
	</n:p>
	<daterangebox allowEmpty="end" endPlaceholder="(open ended)"/>

	<n:h1>Today link and week-of-year</n:h1>
	<daterangebox showTodayLink="true" weekOfYear="true"/>

	<n:h1>Handling the change event</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	the range commits via onChange, carried by a RangeChangeEvent (not an
	InputEvent) - read getRange() / getBegin() / getEnd()
	</n:p>
	<daterangebox id="booking"
		onChange='picked.setValue("From " + event.getBegin() + " to " + event.getEnd())'/>
	<label id="picked"/>

	<n:h1>Disabled and readonly</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	disabled greys out the whole component; readonly keeps the popup usable but
	the inputs are not editable by typing
	</n:p>
	<daterangebox disabled="true" beginValue="${defaultBegin}" endValue="${defaultEnd}"/>
	<daterangebox readonly="true" beginValue="${defaultBegin}" endValue="${defaultEnd}"/>

	<n:h1>Use Cases</n:h1>
	<n:p>
	Three enterprise screens, each built around one Daterangebox. Only the picker and
	the numbers it drives are real; the module header, the field labels and the framing
	are plain text and CSS, so every block stays short enough to read.
	</n:p>

	<style>
		.uc-card {
			width: 720px;
			margin-bottom: 8px;
			border: 1px solid #d5dbe1;
			border-radius: 6px;
			background: #fff;
		}
		.uc-card .z-label { font-size: 13px; }
		.uc-crumb {
			padding: 6px 12px;
			border-radius: 5px 5px 0 0;
			background: #2f4a63;
			color: #c9d8e6;
			font-size: 12px;
			letter-spacing: .04em;
		}
		.uc-crumb b { color: #fff; }
		.uc-band {
			padding: 10px 12px;
			background: #f5f7f9;
			border-bottom: 1px solid #e3e8ec;
		}
		.uc-body { padding: 12px; }
		.uc-note {
			padding: 8px 12px;
			border-top: 1px solid #eef1f4;
			color: #6b7785;
			font-size: 12px;
		}
		.uc-card .uc-key { font-size: 12px; color: #6b7785; }
		.uc-card .uc-value { font-weight: bold; }
		.uc-amount {
			display: block;
			text-align: right;
			font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		}
		.uc-footer { color: #33475b; font-weight: bold; }
		.uc-ok { color: #1a7f37; font-weight: bold; }
		.uc-bad { color: #b3261e; font-weight: bold; }
		.uc-slot {
			display: block;
			padding: 3px 0 3px 8px;
			border-left: 3px solid #8b9aa8;
			font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		}
		.uc-slot-freeze { border-left-color: #b3261e; }
	</style>

	<zscript><![CDATA[
		/* java.util.Calendar has to be imported explicitly: zscript already imports
		   org.zkoss.zul.*, and that package holds the Calendar *component*. */
		import java.util.Calendar;

		java.text.SimpleDateFormat DAY = new java.text.SimpleDateFormat("yyyy/MM/dd");
		java.text.SimpleDateFormat STAMP = new java.text.SimpleDateFormat("MM/dd HH:mm");
		java.text.DecimalFormat MONEY = new java.text.DecimalFormat("#,##0.00");

		Date atMidnight(Calendar c) {
			c.set(Calendar.HOUR_OF_DAY, 0);
			c.set(Calendar.MINUTE, 0);
			c.set(Calendar.SECOND, 0);
			c.set(Calendar.MILLISECOND, 0);
			return c.getTime();
		}
		Date midnight(int daysFromToday) {
			Calendar c = Calendar.getInstance();
			c.add(Calendar.DAY_OF_MONTH, daysFromToday);
			return atMidnight(c);
		}
		Date at(int daysFromToday, int hour) {
			Calendar c = Calendar.getInstance();
			c.add(Calendar.DAY_OF_MONTH, daysFromToday);
			atMidnight(c);
			c.set(Calendar.HOUR_OF_DAY, hour);
			return c.getTime();
		}

		/* ---- ERP: posted journal lines, dated relative to today ---- */
		List GL_LINES = new ArrayList();
		void gl(int daysAgo, String doc, String account, double amount) {
			GL_LINES.add(new Object[] { midnight(-daysAgo), doc, account,
					new Double(amount) });
		}
		gl(0, "JV-000231", "6100 Freight out", 12480.00);
		gl(1, "JV-000230", "5010 Raw material", 184200.00);
		gl(5, "JV-000219", "6210 Utilities", 33910.50);
		gl(12, "JV-000198", "1210 Accounts receivable", 428000.00);
		gl(20, "JV-000154", "5300 Subcontracting", 96750.00);
		gl(34, "JV-000121", "6100 Freight out", 8120.75);
		gl(41, "JV-000098", "5010 Raw material", 211640.00);
		gl(58, "JV-000067", "6300 Depreciation", 74000.00);
		gl(75, "JV-000024", "1210 Accounts receivable", 512300.00);

		void glApply(Date begin, Date end) {
			glRows.getChildren().clear();
			double total = 0;
			int matched = 0;
			for (int i = 0; i < GL_LINES.size(); i++) {
				Object[] line = (Object[]) GL_LINES.get(i);
				Date posted = (Date) line[0];
				if (posted.before(begin) || posted.after(end))
					continue;
				double amount = ((Double) line[3]).doubleValue();
				Row row = new Row();
				row.appendChild(new Label(DAY.format(posted)));
				row.appendChild(new Label((String) line[1]));
				row.appendChild(new Label((String) line[2]));
				Label money = new Label(MONEY.format(amount));
				money.setSclass("uc-amount");
				row.appendChild(money);
				glRows.appendChild(row);
				total += amount;
				matched++;
			}
			long days = DateRange.of(begin, end).getDays().orElse(0);
			glFooter.setValue(matched + " line(s) over " + days + " day(s)"
					+ "  |  total " + MONEY.format(total));
		}
		void glPreset(int monthsBack) {
			Calendar c = Calendar.getInstance();
			c.add(Calendar.MONTH, -monthsBack);
			c.set(Calendar.DAY_OF_MONTH, 1);
			Date begin = atMidnight(c);
			c.set(Calendar.DAY_OF_MONTH, c.getActualMaximum(Calendar.DAY_OF_MONTH));
			Date end = atMidnight(c);
			Date today = midnight(0);
			if (end.after(today))
				end = today;
			glRange.setValue(DateRange.of(begin, end));
			glApply(begin, end);
		}
		void glQuarterToDate() {
			Calendar c = Calendar.getInstance();
			c.set(Calendar.DAY_OF_MONTH, 1);
			c.set(Calendar.MONTH, (c.get(Calendar.MONTH) / 3) * 3);
			Date begin = atMidnight(c);
			Date end = midnight(0);
			glRange.setValue(DateRange.of(begin, end));
			glApply(begin, end);
		}

		/* ---- HR: leave request ---- */
		int LEAVE_BALANCE = 8;
		/* allowEmpty="none" rejects a half-assigned range, so the initial value goes in
		   as one DateRange rather than as beginValue plus endValue. */
		DateRange leaveDates = DateRange.of(midnight(7), midnight(11));

		void leaveQuote(Date begin, Date end) {
			int working = 0;
			Calendar c = Calendar.getInstance();
			c.setTime(begin);
			while (!c.getTime().after(end)) {
				int dow = c.get(Calendar.DAY_OF_WEEK);
				if (dow != Calendar.SATURDAY && dow != Calendar.SUNDAY)
					working++;
				c.add(Calendar.DAY_OF_MONTH, 1);
			}
			long calendarDays = DateRange.of(begin, end).getDays().orElse(0);
			leaveSpan.setValue(DAY.format(begin) + " to " + DAY.format(end)
					+ "  |  " + calendarDays + " calendar day(s), "
					+ working + " working day(s)");
			int left = LEAVE_BALANCE - working;
			if (left < 0) {
				leaveBalance.setSclass("uc-bad");
				leaveBalance.setValue("Over the entitlement by " + (-left)
						+ " working day(s) - unpaid leave needs a separate form");
				leaveSubmit.setDisabled(true);
			} else {
				leaveBalance.setSclass("uc-ok");
				leaveBalance.setValue(working + " day(s) deducted, " + left
						+ " of " + LEAVE_BALANCE + " day(s) left");
				leaveSubmit.setDisabled(false);
			}
		}

		/* ---- Plant maintenance: windows already booked on the line ---- */
		List MW_BOOKED = new ArrayList();
		void booked(String what, Date begin, Date end, boolean freeze) {
			MW_BOOKED.add(new Object[] { what, DateRange.of(begin, end),
					Boolean.valueOf(freeze) });
		}
		booked("WO-8842 Firmware upgrade", at(3, 22), at(4, 6), false);
		booked("WO-8851 Conveyor overhaul", at(9, 0), at(11, 18), false);
		booked("Quarter-end freeze, no changes", at(20, 0), at(24, 23), true);

		DateRange mwWindow = DateRange.of(at(1, 22), at(2, 6));

		void mwCheck(Date begin, Date end) {
			DateRange picked = DateRange.of(begin, end);
			String clash = null;
			for (int i = 0; i < MW_BOOKED.size(); i++) {
				Object[] slot = (Object[]) MW_BOOKED.get(i);
				if (picked.overlaps((DateRange) slot[1])) {
					clash = (String) slot[0];
					break;
				}
			}
			long hours = (end.getTime() - begin.getTime()) / 3600000L;
			if (clash != null) {
				mwStatus.setSclass("uc-bad");
				mwStatus.setValue("Rejected - the window overlaps " + clash);
				mwSubmit.setDisabled(true);
			} else {
				mwStatus.setSclass("uc-ok");
				mwStatus.setValue("Line 2 is free - " + hours
						+ " h of planned downtime");
				mwSubmit.setDisabled(false);
			}
		}
	]]></zscript>

	<n:h2>ERP: posting-date inquiry on the general ledger</n:h2>
	<n:p>
	The range is the query. Presets write it with setValue(DateRange), which smart-updates
	both inputs, so the buttons and the calendar drive the same state; the grid is
	rebuilt from whatever getBegin()/getEnd() report. Two attributes carry the accounting
	rules: constraint="no future" keeps the inquiry out of unposted periods, and
	maxNights="92" stops an accidental full-year scan at one quarter.
	</n:p>
	<div sclass="uc-card">
		<n:div class="uc-crumb">FIN &#8250; General Ledger &#8250; <n:b>Journal Inquiry (GL-3200)</n:b></n:div>
		<div sclass="uc-band">
			<hlayout valign="middle" spacing="10px">
				<label sclass="uc-key" value="Company"/>
				<label sclass="uc-value" value="1000 Acme Manufacturing"/>
				<label sclass="uc-key" value="Posting date"/>
				<daterangebox id="glRange" width="300px" allowEmpty="none"
							  constraint="no future" maxNights="92" showTodayLink="true"
							  separator=" &#8594; "
							  onChange="glApply(event.getBegin(), event.getEnd())"/>
			</hlayout>
			<hlayout valign="middle" spacing="10px">
				<label sclass="uc-key" value="Period"/>
				<button label="This month" onClick="glPreset(0)"/>
				<button label="Last month" onClick="glPreset(1)"/>
				<button label="Quarter to date" onClick="glQuarterToDate()"/>
			</hlayout>
		</div>
		<div sclass="uc-body">
			<grid width="100%" emptyMessage="No journal lines posted in this range">
				<columns>
					<column label="Posting date" width="110px"/>
					<column label="Document" width="110px"/>
					<column label="Account"/>
					<column label="Amount" width="130px" align="right"/>
				</columns>
				<rows id="glRows"/>
			</grid>
			<label id="glFooter" sclass="uc-footer"/>
		</div>
		<n:div class="uc-note">
			Try a range wider than a quarter: the component refuses it with an error box
			before any listener runs, so the query never reaches the ledger.
		</n:div>
	</div>
	<zscript>glPreset(0);</zscript>

	<n:h2>HR: leave request bounded by policy</n:h2>
	<n:p>
	Here the range is the form's only real input, and the attributes are the leave policy:
	constraint="no past" blocks a backdated request, allowEmpty="none" makes both endpoints
	mandatory, and maxNights="20" is the cap on a single application. Everything below the
	picker is priced in onChange - the calendar-day count comes from DateRange.getDays(),
	the deduction only counts working days, and going over the entitlement disables Submit.
	</n:p>
	<div sclass="uc-card">
		<n:div class="uc-crumb">HR &#8250; Time Off &#8250; <n:b>Leave Request (HR-204)</n:b></n:div>
		<div sclass="uc-band">
			<hlayout valign="middle" spacing="10px">
				<label sclass="uc-key" value="Employee"/>
				<label sclass="uc-value" value="E-10427 Jane Chen"/>
				<label sclass="uc-key" value="Manager"/>
				<label sclass="uc-value" value="Mark Lee"/>
				<label sclass="uc-key" value="Balance"/>
				<label sclass="uc-value" value="${LEAVE_BALANCE} working day(s)"/>
			</hlayout>
		</div>
		<div sclass="uc-body">
			<vlayout spacing="6px">
				<hlayout valign="middle" spacing="10px">
					<label sclass="uc-key" value="Leave type"/>
					<combobox readonly="true" width="150px" value="Annual leave">
						<comboitem label="Annual leave"/>
						<comboitem label="Sick leave"/>
						<comboitem label="Unpaid leave"/>
					</combobox>
					<label sclass="uc-key" value="Dates"/>
					<daterangebox id="leaveRange" width="300px" constraint="no past" allowEmpty="none"
								  maxNights="20" numberOfMonths="2"
								  beginPlaceholder="First day" endPlaceholder="Last day"
								  separator=" &#8594; "
								  value="${leaveDates}"
								  onChange="leaveQuote(event.getBegin(), event.getEnd())"/>
				</hlayout>
				<label id="leaveSpan"/>
				<label id="leaveBalance"/>
				<button id="leaveSubmit" label="Submit for approval"
						onClick="Clients.showNotification('Request routed to Mark Lee',
								'info', null, 'end_center', 3000)"/>
			</vlayout>
		</div>
		<n:div class="uc-note">
			Weekends are still selectable - the policy counts them, it does not forbid them,
			so the working-day math belongs in the listener rather than in a constraint.
		</n:div>
	</div>
	<zscript>leaveQuote(leaveDates.getBegin(), leaveDates.getEnd());</zscript>

	<n:h2>Plant maintenance: a downtime window that must not collide</n:h2>
	<n:p>
	showTime="true" because downtime is booked in hours, not days. The picked range arrives
	as a DateRange, so the collision check against what is already scheduled is one call -
	DateRange.overlaps() - over the same kind of object, and the quarter-end freeze is just
	one more range in that list. Note that overlaps() treats both endpoints as inclusive: a
	window starting exactly when another ends still counts as a collision. The listener can
	assume the window points forward: the times carry over from the previous pick, and the
	component rejects a begin later than the end before onChange is fired.
	</n:p>
	<div sclass="uc-card">
		<n:div class="uc-crumb">PM &#8250; Assets &#8250; <n:b>Maintenance Window (PM-1105)</n:b></n:div>
		<div sclass="uc-band">
			<hlayout valign="middle" spacing="10px">
				<label sclass="uc-key" value="Asset"/>
				<label sclass="uc-value" value="LINE-02 Bottling line 2"/>
				<label sclass="uc-key" value="Plant"/>
				<label sclass="uc-value" value="TPE-01"/>
			</hlayout>
		</div>
		<div sclass="uc-body">
			<vlayout spacing="6px">
				<label sclass="uc-key" value="Already booked on this asset"/>
				<vlayout id="mwBooked" spacing="2px"/>
				<hlayout valign="middle" spacing="10px">
					<label sclass="uc-key" value="Requested window"/>
					<daterangebox id="mwRange" showTime="true" constraint="no past"
								  allowEmpty="none" maxNights="7" numberOfMonths="2"
								  separator=" &#8594; "
								  value="${mwWindow}"
								  onChange="mwCheck(event.getBegin(), event.getEnd())"/>
				</hlayout>
				<label id="mwStatus"/>
				<button id="mwSubmit" label="Request downtime"
						onClick="Clients.showNotification('Window sent to the shift supervisor',
								'info', null, 'end_center', 3000)"/>
			</vlayout>
		</div>
		<n:div class="uc-note">
			Pick dates inside the second booked window above to see the request rejected,
			and drag across the freeze period to see the same check catch a policy block.
		</n:div>
	</div>
	<zscript><![CDATA[
		for (int i = 0; i < MW_BOOKED.size(); i++) {
			Object[] slot = (Object[]) MW_BOOKED.get(i);
			DateRange r = (DateRange) slot[1];
			Label line = new Label(STAMP.format(r.getBegin()) + "  -  "
					+ STAMP.format(r.getEnd()) + "    " + slot[0]);
			line.setSclass(((Boolean) slot[2]).booleanValue()
					? "uc-slot uc-slot-freeze" : "uc-slot");
			line.setParent(mwBooked);
		}
		mwCheck(mwWindow.getBegin(), mwWindow.getEnd());
	]]></zscript>
</zk>
